abstract: >
  A reusable toolkit for running a self-hosted, sovereign git server (Forgejo)
  with disciplined, dogfooded workflows: own-and-mirror, contribute-back relay,
  follow-copy upstream mirroring, and controlled declassified release; with
  SHA-verified mirroring, GPG/sha256-verified server updates, encrypted backups,
  and a fail-closed confidentiality leak-gate. Initiated by Raazesh Sainudiin in
  the Open Earth Network, with development funding from VakeWorks AB.
keywords:
  - sovereign-git
  - digital-sovereignty
  - forgejo
  - git-mirroring
  - self-hosting
  - supply-chain-verification
